# Project documentation, kept on disk and out of the repo. None of it is read by the
# build. A fresh clone without these loses the signing-key procedure and the longer
# notes on design and voice, so keep your copies. The exceptions are committed: the root
# README.md is the repo's front page, and apps/README.md and guides/README.md are the
# schema and writing rules for the content beside them (the content glob skips both).
BRIEF.md
DEPLOY.md
DESIGN.md
ROADMAP.md
tools/sample-output/README.md

# Working material for whoever is art-directing the globe. Same reasoning as the block
# above: it is documentation and reference, the build never reads it, and the reference
# stills are ~5MB of PNG that regenerate from the running site in one command
# (node tools/capture-globe.mjs). tools/capture-globe.mjs itself IS committed — the
# script is the reproducible part, the pictures are not.
HANDOFF-VISUAL.md
handoff/
